  "enunciado": "A utility map divides a rail yard into twenty-five work zones. Color each region with red, green or blue. A region pair separated by a dash denotes a direct link. Linked regions must have different colors. The links work both ways. The regions are Bridge, Cabin, Crane, Depot, Fence, Furnace, Gantry, Gate, Lane, Loop, Platform, Point, Ramp, Relay, Shed, Siding, Signal, Station, Switch, Tower, Track, Trench, Tunnel, Viaduct, Workshop.\n1. Switch is green.\n2. Signal is red.\n3. Switch–Tunnel.\n4. Signal–Switch, Signal–Tower, Signal–Tunnel, Signal–Workshop.\n5. Siding–Switch, Siding–Track, Siding–Tunnel, Siding–Viaduct.\n6. Track–Tunnel.\n7. Cabin–Crane, Cabin–Signal, Cabin–Track.\n8. Platform–Switch, Platform–Tunnel.\n9. Tower–Track, Tower–Viaduct, Tower–Workshop.\n10. Furnace–Point, Furnace–Signal, Furnace–Station, Furnace–Tunnel.\n11. Gate–Signal, Gate–Switch, Gate–Trench.\n12. Station–Tower.\n13. Loop–Tower, Loop–Viaduct.\n14. Relay–Station, Relay–Track, Relay–Trench.\n15. Depot–Furnace, Depot–Gantry, Depot–Signal.\n16. Crane–Fence, Crane–Gate, Crane–Platform.\n17. Fence–Gantry, Fence–Point, Fence–Relay, Fence–Tower.\n18. Bridge–Relay, Bridge–Trench, Bridge–Viaduct, Bridge–Workshop.\n19. Shed–Signal, Shed–Viaduct, Shed–Workshop.\n20. Ramp–Relay, Ramp–Switch.\n21. Gantry–Siding.\n22. Lane–Ramp, Lane–Track, Lane–Trench.\nFor each named region, give its color.",
